# Generated module tree (regenerate on-demand: npm run generate:module-tree)
module_tree_full.md
# Generated engine type-resolution map (scripts/gen-engine-tsconfig-paths.mjs, via
# pretype-check / pretest / prebuild). Tracking it made every fresh clone inherit one
# machine's sibling-repo path - a `paths` entry pointing at a directory the reader does
# not have. Untracked, it is regenerated to whatever is correct locally: working-copy
# engine when a usable checkout exists, otherwise no engine paths at all so `tsc`
# resolves the published packages from node_modules.
tsconfig.engine-paths.json

# Generated peggy parser (scripts/gen-pine-parser.ts, via gen:pine-parser /
# pretype-check / pretest / prebuild / prewatch). The .js is ~5,400 lines of
# codegen; it stays untracked, and `parser.generated.d.ts` (committed) is what
# `tsc` resolves. Why generated at build instead of `peggy.generate` at runtime:
# peggy 5 compiles with eval, which CSP `script-src 'self'` forbids - the chart
# then silently failed to restore saved Pine scripts (measured 2026-10-17,
# verify-pine 5/13 on staging).
src/lib/pinescript/parser.generated.js
packages/vn-kline-widget-pro/src/pinescript/parser.generated.js

# License signing keys. `scripts/issue-license.js --gen-keypair` writes the PRIVATE jwk
# here (never to stdout - see the step in ci.yml that asserts it). A committed private
# key signs licenses for the vendor, so losing this file to git is worse than losing the
# file. The PUBLIC jwk is safe to track: it is embedded in the shipped bundle on purpose.
*.key
license.key
*.jwk

# AI Agents
.agents/
# `.opencode/` holds local tooling state (plugins, its own package-lock) that must not be
# tracked. The SKILL handbooks are the exception: they are process documentation, and a
# rule that points at an untracked file is decoration - the next clone would have a
# Planning Gate referencing a skill that is not there (docs/upgrade-standard/
# AGENT_PROTOCOL.md "Planning Gate"). Note the `/*` form: git will not descend into an
# ignored DIRECTORY, so negating a child of `.opencode/` alone would never match.
.opencode/*
!.opencode/skills/
# 2026-10-20 (agent harness P2): the plugin directory must be tracked too. A rule that points
# at an untracked plugin is decoration: the next clone would have `AGENTS.md` pointing at a
# plugin that is not there. Same `/*` rule as above - negate the DIRECTORY, not a child of it.
!.opencode/plugins/
# Agent slice state (plan on disk) - machine-local, never committed.
.planning/

# F-24: test outputs and ephemeral artifacts
test-output.*
*.junit.xml
videos/*.webm
.blackboxrules
test-minimal.test.ts


# tsup/tsc declaration byproducts inside widget-pro src (regenerated by build;
# the committed parser.generated.d.ts below stays tracked regardless)
packages/vn-kline-widget-pro/src/**/*.d.ts
!packages/vn-kline-widget-pro/src/pinescript/parser.generated.d.ts
